\section*{ALE singularities: Type-II existence and a bounded-scalar scale-energy certificate}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Four-dimensional Ricci-flow extension}: The paper claims smooth continuation of a Ricci flow on a closed four-manifold through any finite time at which scalar curvature stays uniformly bounded. The continuation occurs on the same manifold.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Four-dimensional Ricci-flow extension}: Outermost concentration scales produce buffered time patches and finite Ricci-flat bubble trees. Parabolic annular estimates and a time maximal function convert spacetime Ricci energy into the static weighted error of a companion elliptic theorem. Comparing positive functional variation with static smallness forces the root energy to vanish, contradicting the selected change of concentration scale.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Four-dimensional Ricci-flow extension}: The four-dimensional extension theorem excludes ALE singularities in the additional bounded-scalar setting, but the ALE question does not impose bounded scalar curvature.

This page records partial support. Complete resolution of the catalogue question is not established by this record.

\subsection{Formal verification}
\textit{Four-dimensional Ricci-flow extension}: The pinned catalogue lists no Lean formalization for this result.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Bounded scalar curvature and smooth extension of four-dimensional Ricci flow}, 2026-09-24; citation key \texttt{OAI:Bounded-scalar-curvature-and-smooth-extension-of-four-dimensional-Ricci-flow-September-24-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Bounded-scalar-curvature-and-smooth-extension-of-four-dimensional-Ricci-flow-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Bounded-scalar-curvature-and-smooth-extension-of-four-dimensional-Ricci-flow-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Bounded-scalar-curvature-and-smooth-extension-of-four-dimensional-Ricci-flow-September-24-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Bounded-scalar-curvature-and-smooth-extension-of-four-dimensional-Ricci-flow-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
